  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe maintainer's rule on #3748: Helix, Ramp and Plunge stay lead-in types. Arc in the cut plane (the #3746 entry from the air) is the recommended entry for \"Pass starts at\" Inside and Outside. A non-recommended choice gives a warning.\n\n- `sim::verify`: new advisory `Warning::EntryNotRecommended { at, entry, inside }` and the one sentence `entry_advice` (selected type, recommended Arc, reason). The warning does not hold the post. MCP kind: `entry_not_recommended`.\n- `motion`: where the Arc entry from the air applies (the air room exists) and the user selected Inside or Outside with Helix, Ramp or Plunge, the ladder (`pocket.rs`, `pocket_avoid.rs`) writes one `entry:` note. The entry runs as selected. Auto and an Adaptive op get no advice.\n- `app`: `operation::entry_not_recommended` turns the note into the one warning. The status line counts it.\n- `ui`: the Lead in / Lead out page of 2D Offset greys nothing out. With Inside or Outside and Helix, Ramp or Plunge, it shows the same sentence as a visible line under the Type selector.\n- Removed the automatic #3577 dead-end ramp: `level_ramp_entry.rs` (`dead_end_ramp`, `too_short_at`, `stand_in_note`), the `ramp_starts` marks and plumbing, and `StartSide::ramp_fallback_note`.\n\nWhat was left of the automatic ramp on `main` (ed6f980ef): #3744 had already stopped the marks round a part, and #3790 stopped the #3567 dead ends there. The ramp was still live for the pocket form of Outside (`!around_part`, no stock known). A later pass there now takes the pass link's entry, which is the user's (#2265 restart). #3746's named stand-in for a selected Arc (a helix, then a ramp, each named) stays.\n\n**Overlap:** this PR touches `ladder_links.rs::pass_link`. It deletes only the `dead_end_ramp` call block (old lines 187-195). The #3837 Clearance arm is kept (origin/main merged, no conflict).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `motion` `pass_start_engagement`: `a_selected_entry_is_kept_and_named_once` (pin 1), `the_arc_entry_has_no_helix_or_ramp_and_no_advice` (pin 2), `start_side_pass_has_no_automatic_ramp` (pin 3), `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` (no ramp exemption, round a part), `a_short_dead_end_no_longer_falls_back_to_auto`.\n- `app` `offset_pass_start`: `entry_advice::the_advice_note_posts_one_advisory_warning`; heavy `entry_advice::fig8_outside_selected_helix_warns_once_and_arc_not_at_all`.\n- `ui` lib: `the_leads_tab_advises_arc_next_to_the_entry_type_for_inside_and_outside` (pin 4; the Type combo is not disabled; the `#[test]` count of camcraft-ui goes up by one).\n- `sim` lib: `the_advice_names_the_selected_and_the_recommended_type`.\n\nRed first: pins 1 and 4 and the app and sim pins use the new advice API and the new warning, so they cannot pass on `main`. Pins 2 and 3 round a part were not run on `main`; #3744 and #3746 can already make them green there.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate `--base origin/main` (384 steps, 55.6 min): 1 failed, `app:adaptive_pass_start` (an Adaptive op on its ring fallback got the advice). Fixed in abfaf7884; the suite then passed (4 of 4). The other 383 steps passed on the head before that fix.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on the final head.\n- Heavy: `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: offset_pass_start\"` on the final head: ok, 7 passed (known-fail #3825 skipped by the gate).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick gate was not run again after abfaf7884 (one condition in two files).\n- The light lane and other heavy lanes.\n- No app window was opened.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/3748-entry-warnings.md`. The 2D Offset seed stays Helix; follow-up #3843 owns an Arc default for Inside and Outside.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside: a selected Helix, Ramp or Plunge lead-in is kept and gives one warning that recommends Arc (also shown on the Lead in / Lead out page); the automatic dead-end ramp is removed.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3748\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
